From dd945a920d51114115e19e42fe3b7a19c0382026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:58:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Eden (Doris): NCE: the game's reads of memory a GPU drawing
 covers get the drawing (setting, on by default)

With the JIT and reactive flushing, Eden copies a texture the GPU drew into guest memory before
the game's code reads it there. With NCE the game's code runs natively and reads guest memory
directly, so it got what was there before the drawing. TotK reads GPU drawings back (reports:
ground corrupting into other ground and grass vanishing on NCE, gone with the JIT and reactive
flushing).

New Doris setting doris_nce_gpu_reads (default 1). When a tracked texture becomes GPU-drawn, its
pages that the GPU caches track are made unreadable for NCE code. A read or write that stops
there is told apart by the ESR in the signal frame: the drawing is copied into guest memory
(GPU::OnCPURead, as reactive flushing does: the first time it waits for the GPU, afterwards the
texture is copied at fences), then reads go on with the page read-only (writes still go through
Eden's invalidation) and writes go on to the invalidation. Pages the caches stop tracking are
forgotten. The report counts the pages, reads and writes, and the time the game waited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
